{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1455943-what-happens-to-the-great-pacific-garbage-patch-if-collum-dies","id":1455943,"title":"What happens to the Great Pacific garbage patch if Collum dies?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-01T11:18:05-07:00","id":1455943,"title":"What happens to the Great Pacific garbage patch if Collum dies?","content":"If you kill the Maeljin Incarna of Sludge, what exactly disappears? How degraded does our waste have to be before it gets sucked into Malfeas to fill the spiritual void that has been left behind? I assume the melted goops of plastic in our ocean counts as sludge, since it surely is an element of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 08-01-2021, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T13:51:24-07:00","id":1455950,"title":"","content":"Nothing disappears. Killing spirits doesn't magically get rid of their material correspondences. Efforts to clean up pollution and reducing it building back up would get easier without the influence of said spirits, but someone would still have to actually do that work (and for high level spirits like the Maeljin, it's questionable if you can truly kill them for good while said material correspondences persist).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-01T14:20:55-07:00","id":1455955,"title":"","content":"\u201cDestroying one of the elemental Maeljin Incarna would increase the difficulty of summoning that type of elemental by at least +4 (difficulties over 10 make the summoning impossible) everywhere \ud835\udc1a\ud835\udc27\ud835\udc1d \ud835\udc30\ud835\udc28\ud835\udc2e\ud835\udc25\ud835\udc1d \ud835\udc27\ud835\udc28\ud835\udc2d\ud835\udc22\ud835\udc1c\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc1a\ud835\udc1b\ud835\udc25\ud835\udc32 \ud835\udc1d\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc1c\ud835\udc2b\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc1a\ud835\udc2c\ud835\udc1e \ud835\udc2d\ud835\udc21\ud835\udc1e \ud835\udc1a\ud835\udc26\ud835\udc28\ud835\udc2e\ud835\udc27\ud835\udc2d \ud835\udc1a\ud835\udc27\ud835\udc1d \ud835\udc2f\ud835\udc22\ud835\udc2b\ud835\udc2e\ud835\udc25\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc27\ud835\udc1c\ud835\udc1e \ud835\udc28\ud835\udc1f \ud835\udc2d\ud835\udc21\ud835\udc1e \ud835\udc1a\ud835\udc1c\ud835\udc2d\ud835\udc2e\ud835\udc1a\ud835\udc25 \ud835\udc29\ud835\udc21\ud835\udc32\ud835\udc2c\ud835\udc22\ud835\udc1c\ud835\udc1a\ud835\udc25 \ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc25\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc26\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc27\ud835\udc2d \ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc2f\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc2b\ud835\udc32-\ud835\udc30\ud835\udc21\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc2b\ud835\udc1e \ud835\udc28\ud835\udc27 \ud835\udc04\ud835\udc1a\ud835\udc2b\ud835\udc2d\ud835\udc21.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c The palaces of the four elemental Maeljin sit near the center of each Duchy. <b> \ud835\udc03\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc2c\ud835\udc2d\ud835\udc2b\ud835\udc28\ud835\udc32\ud835\udc22\ud835\udc27\ud835\udc20 \ud835\udc28\ud835\udc27\ud835\udc1e \ud835\udc28\ud835\udc1f \ud835\udc2d\ud835\udc21\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc2c\ud835\udc1e \ud835\udc1c\ud835\udc1a\ud835\udc2c\ud835\udc2d\ud835\udc25\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc2c \ud835\udc28\ud835\udc1f \ud835\udc1c\ud835\udc28\ud835\udc2b\ud835\udc2b\ud835\udc2e\ud835\udc29\ud835\udc2d\ud835\udc22\ud835\udc28\ud835\udc27 \ud835\udc26\ud835\udc22\ud835\udc20\ud835\udc21\ud835\udc2d \ud835\udc30\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc1a\ud835\udc24\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc27 \ud835\udc2d\ud835\udc21\ud835\udc1e \ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc25\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc26\ud835\udc1e\ud835\udc27\ud835\udc2d, </b> especially if the Garou also permanently destroy the elemental Maeljin.\u201d<br /> <br /> It says it would decrease the AMOUNT of that element as well as it\u2019s virulence. I am just wondering by how much. Remember, if you destroy an objects spirit, that object tends to not so slowly disintegrate. The example I remember was if a car\u2019s spirit is removed or destroyed then it might technically still work for a few days, but it will fall apart very quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 08-02-2021, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T13:21:30-07:00","id":1456149,"title":"","content":"That will vary from ST to ST obviously but personnaly in a WTA campaign who involved killing Choke I considered the exploit sufficient to significantly lower the amount of pollutants in the air. Reality's explanation for that was these elements became suddenly degradable/absorbable. Killing Collum in this paradigm would cause the plastic patch to slowly dissolve into saltwater, leaving people fumble for a rational explanation.<br /> <br /> Spiritually it would mean the element has much more chances to be empty and without a spiritual counterpart. Which would allows Gaian spirits to quickly destroy it from the other side of the Gauntlet. (Go team Cockroach and Rat)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T18:10:53-07:00","id":1456157,"title":"","content":"If you're going after a giant patch of plastic, you'd probably want to look into plastic-spirits rather than elemental sludge. And that's going to be a harder thing to take on, because plastic-spirits can recruit an awful lot more sympathetic and widespread support.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T21:19:55-07:00","id":1456162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1455943-what-happens-to-the-great-pacific-garbage-patch-if-collum-dies?p=1456157#post1456157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going after a giant patch of plastic, you'd probably want to look into plastic-spirits rather than elemental sludge. And that's going to be a harder thing to take on, because plastic-spirits can recruit an awful lot more sympathetic and widespread support.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but plastic melts in the ocean. Sometimes just into pure goop. If it has been out in the ocean and the sun for a while, it should at least corrode and melt somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-04T23:47:22-07:00","id":1456164,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd say you'd mainly be dealing with Plastic Elementals. Many of them would probably be Wyrm tainted. And you'd have other types of spirits and Elementals mixed in as well. Still, I think the effects if destroying Collum would be fairly marginal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T01:36:01-07:00","id":1456219,"title":"","content":"At an absolute stretch, if you somehow nuked all the relevant spirits, things would get maybe 50% less bad. &quot;less bad&quot; doesn't necessarily mean you'll half the mass of bottles in the ocean, perhaps instead they'll stop releasing microplastics or will smell better or fish will learn to avoid that shit or some mix thereof. But the spiritual side is only half (hence 50%) of the equation, This said:<br /> 1: so long as the material is around in large quantities, new spirits will generate. <br /> 2; Killing the Incarnae has an impact on the other spirits, but you're not killing the whole family by killing the head. Many other banes exist, and they will use this power vacume to promote themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T08:54:05-07:00","id":1456243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1455943-what-happens-to-the-great-pacific-garbage-patch-if-collum-dies?p=1456164#post1456164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd say you'd mainly be dealing with Plastic Elementals. Many of them would probably be Wyrm tainted. And you'd have other types of spirits and Elementals mixed in as well. Still, I think the effects if destroying Collum would be fairly marginal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I thought killing the Maeljin Incarna was an event that would shake the globe. At least that is how BotW presented it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T09:34:46-07:00","id":1456248,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to note that offing the Maeljin has a lasting effect, when most other Celestines just nominate the next Jaggling in line for a promotion to fill the position, and oddly enough, very little seems to get through to a physical effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1455943-what-happens-to-the-great-pacific-garbage-patch-if-collum-dies?p=1456243#post1456243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I thought killing the Maeljin Incarna was an event that would shake the globe. At least that is how BotW presented it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Find a really high-profile plastic elemental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T12:39:49-07:00","id":1456254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1455943-what-happens-to-the-great-pacific-garbage-patch-if-collum-dies?p=1456248#post1456248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting to note that offing the Maeljin has a lasting effect, when most other Celestines just nominate the next Jaggling in line for a promotion to fill the position, and oddly enough, very little seems to get through to a physical effect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Find a really high-profile plastic elemental.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand it's less offing the Maeljin but doing so in a symbolic manner who destroys the position. It's explictly mentionned the Nameless Angel manages to self-destruct and must be replaced by Gree. Some of the most violent Maeljin like the Hellbringer or Lord Steel also have &quot;if you don't destroy them with the appropriate method, you replace them&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T20:18:36-07:00","id":1456275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ganonso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1455943-what-happens-to-the-great-pacific-garbage-patch-if-collum-dies?p=1456254#post1456254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I understand it's less offing the Maeljin but doing so in a symbolic manner who destroys the position. It's explictly mentionned the Nameless Angel manages to self-destruct and must be replaced by Gree. Some of the most violent Maeljin like the Hellbringer or Lord Steel also have &quot;if you don't destroy them with the appropriate method, you replace them&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. There's no other way to off them but that way; old-fashioned killing presumably fails to take out other Incarnae as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}